{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogSineSmoothPart","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.LogSineSmoothPart","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue","lean:module:QOU.Knot.Clausen"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.smooth_defect_squeeze","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.smooth_defect_squeeze","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L280-L312","doc":"**L4-1c(ii) — the smooth half is squeezed (sorry-free).**  Telescoping\nthe per-cell bounds:\n\n    h·( φ_ext(n) − log 2 )  ≤  Σ_{i<n} ∫_{cell_i} (φ(x_{i+1}) − φ(u)) du  ≤  0,\n\nan `O(h)` two-sided bound obtained with **no derivative estimate** — only\nantitonicity of `φ` and the `sin u ≤ u` ceiling.  Together with the exact\nsingular telescope (L4-1c(i)) and Stirling (L4-1b) this closes the\ningredient list for the second-order log-sine expansion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cell_defect_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cell_defect_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L211-L278","doc":"**Per-cell two-sided bound.**  Each cell defect is `≤ 0` (antitonicity)\nand `≥ h·(φ(x_{i+1}) − ceiling_i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.ae_phi_le_phiExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.ae_phi_le_phiExt","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L169-L209","doc":"On each cell, `φ` stays under the cell ceiling — a.e., the single\nexception being `u = 0` in the first cell (where `φ`'s junk value is\nirrelevant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiExt_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiExt_succ","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L165-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiExt_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiExt_zero","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L162-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiExt","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L157-L160","doc":"The cell ceiling: `log 2` for the first cell (whose left endpoint is the\nunusable `0`), the previous grid value thereafter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.intervalIntegrable_phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.intervalIntegrable_phi","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L149-L155","doc":"`φ` is interval-integrable everywhere: both halves are, unconditionally\n(`intervalIntegrable_log'` covers the singularity at `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_le_log_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_le_log_two","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L135-L145","doc":"The first-cell ceiling: `φ(u) ≤ log 2` on `(0, π)` — just `sin u ≤ u`.\nThis stands in for the (unused) value `φ(0⁺) = log 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.strictAntiOn_phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.strictAntiOn_phi","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L110-L133","doc":"**`φ` is strictly antitone on `(0, π)`** — so every cell defect\n`φ(x_j) − φ(u)`, `u ≤ x_j`, is `≤ 0`.  This is the property that\nreplaces the Lipschitz bound the bean expected to need. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_phi","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L99-L108","doc":"`φ` has the expected derivative on `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_sub_mul_cos_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_sub_mul_cos_pos","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L70-L97","doc":"`x·cos x < sin x` on `(0, π)` — the single inequality behind `φ`'s\nmonotonicity.  `ψ(x) = sin x − x·cos x` vanishes at `0` and has\n`ψ'(x) = x·sin x > 0` on the interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSmoothPart.lean#L65-L68","doc":"The smooth part of the log-sine integrand, `φ(x) = log(2 sin x / x)`\nwritten as a difference (so no removable-singularity bookkeeping is\nneeded; the value at `0` is never used). ","signatureChunk":0}]}